        {
          "question": "q-330348",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Suppose ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are both solutions of the homogeneous system\n${x}^{\u2032}(t)=A\\text{\u00a0}x(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same system?\n\n- $x(t)={e}^{t}\\,{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)$\n- $x(t)={x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)$\n- $x(t)={x}_{1}(t)\\times {x}_{2}(t)$ (cross-product)",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066703/state.json",
          "file_sha256": "7a8639649c43ccf473fc0212c91af3b4fdc66d39cbce10b1e9640246157aea6c"
        }
      ],
