        {
          "question": "q-330290",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfy the homogeneous system ${x}^{\u2032}(t)=A\\text{\u00a0}x(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ satisfy the inhomogeneous system\n${x}^{\u2032}(t)=A\\text{\u00a0}x(t)+f(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same inhomogeneous system?\n\n- $3\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$\n- ${x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)+2\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$\n- $-4\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$",
