    {
      "question": "e-21110",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "c0b01f8291a023b85226498c4dfbc2550dde0826a04fc4ac183e5b93a0a064cd",
      "new_sha256": "96107808bc85750d0f65b22b2091841f08dd307074413b424bf3a03faa92700b",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-21110",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if $\\mathbf{x}_{1}(t)$ and $\\mathbf{x}_{2}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system, then for any constants $c_1$ and $c_2,$ the linear combination \n\n$$\nc_{1}\\mathbf{x}_{1}(t)+c_{2}\\mathbf{x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis also a solution of the system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expressions.\n\n- Option I is a solution to the system. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n6 \\cdot \\mathbf{x}_1(t) + (-1) \\cdot \\mathbf{x}_2(t)\n$$\n\nis a linear combination of the solutions $\\mathbf{x}_{1}(t)$ and $\\mathbf{x}_{2}(t)$ with constant multiplies $c_1=6$ and $c_2=-1,$ respectively.\n\n- Option II is a solution to the system. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n-3 \\cdot \\mathbf{x}_1(t) + 4 \\cdot \\mathbf{x}_2(t)\n$$\n\nis a linear combination of the solutions $\\mathbf{x}_{1}(t)$ and $\\mathbf{x}_{2}(t)$ with constant multiplies $c_1=-3$ and $c_2=4,$ respectively.\n\n- Option III might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a linear combination of the solutions $\\mathbf{x}_{1}(t)$ and $\\mathbf{x}_{2}(t).$ Notice that the multipliers of the first and the second terms are not constant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\".",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066703/example-21110.json",
          "file_sha256": "e1862497f5f8f3265314df44fa75c1b3fee9f73fcc42d47710de5270b3d80b06"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 2204,
      "reason": "Observed MA content supersedes the stored value",
