      "new_sha256": "5e6cea17bbdbbcea4d21b42f3deaef35e60ad1f1445b8b00718fb11793e9c496",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-21111",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Let $\\mathbf{x}_1(t)$ and $\\mathbf{x}_2(t)$ satisfy the homogeneous system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\ \\mathbf{x}(t)$ and $\\mathbf{x}_p(t)$ satisfy the inhomogeneous system\n$\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\ \\mathbf{x}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same inhomogeneous system?\n\n- $\\mathbf{x}_1(t) + 2\\cdot \\mathbf{x}_2(t) + \\mathbf{x}_p(t)$\n\n- $4\\cdot \\mathbf{x}_2(t) + \\mathbf{x}_p(t)$\n\n- $-\\mathbf{x}_1(t) - \\mathbf{x}_p(t)$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066703/example-21111.json",
